<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Celle</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Celle is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aller">Aller</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-saxony">Lower Saxony</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the southern edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luneburg">Lüneburg</a> Heath. From the late 14th century it was the residence of the Guelph dukes of Brunswick-Lüneburg ruling the Principality of Lüneburg, whose palace still stands. When the last duke, George William, died in 1705 it passed to the Electorate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a>; its old town keeps hundreds of half-timbered houses.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/celle.jpg" alt="Celle" width="320" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schlosscelle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
